  "native_contract": {
    "entry": "SHIJU_CODEBUDDY_SKILL_ROOT selects the audited SessionSkillView. Nonempty selections require the reviewed executable; empty selections remove all implicit skill levels. Conflicting environment overrides are rejected.",
    "discovery": "Native scanner reads the owned root. Final ProductManager configuration reads (including cached execution snapshots) and session skill merges filter builtin/plugin/user/project skills to the owned root. Model-drivable builtin command fallback is disabled whenever the root marker exists, including empty selections.",
    "activation": "Actual native Skill(skill) result must expose the current body and mounted base directory before actual Read and Bash calls. Current tool descriptions, rather than resumed history, define the catalog.",
    "filesystem": "Canonical selected source reads are allowed through the ACP file bridge. Foreign paths, symlink escape, writes and deny-all remain rejected; full_access is unchanged.",
    "scripts": "The fixed native ACP bridge incorrectly sent a shell expression as terminal/create.command. The reviewed patch sends /bin/sh and args [-c, expression], retaining terminal permission checks.",
    "updates": "Both sources require add/remove/V2/idle update/isolation/cancellation/restart and permission denial. View changes retire the cached CLI; no native hot-reload promise.",
    "isolation_probes": "Both sources include unselected project and private native-home skills. cli_local also loads a real unselected plugin. Catalog names must equal the selected set, excluding native builtin skills. session_model custom launch argument rejection is preserved."
  },
